 559:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 560:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 561:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Reads characters from SEGGER real-time-terminal control block
 562:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    which have been previously stored by the application.
 563:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Do not lock against interrupts and multiple access.
 564:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Used to do the same operation that J-Link does, to transfer 
 565:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    RTT data via other channels, such as TCP/IP or UART.
 566:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 567:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 568:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of Up-buffer to be used.
 569:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to buffer provided by target application, to copy characters from RTT-up-
 570:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferSize   Size of the target application buffer.
 571:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 572:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
 573:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes that have been read.
 574:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 575:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Additional information
 576:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    This function must not be called when J-Link might also do RTT.
 577:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
