 743:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccRade8p.s 			page 30


 744:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_ReadUpBuffer
 745:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 746:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 747:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Reads characters from SEGGER real-time-terminal control block
 748:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    which have been previously stored by the application.
 749:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Used to do the same operation that J-Link does, to transfer 
 750:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    RTT data via other channels, such as TCP/IP or UART.
 751:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 752:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 753:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of Up-buffer to be used.
 754:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to buffer provided by target application, to copy characters from RTT-up-
 755:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferSize   Size of the target application buffer.
 756:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 757:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
 758:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes that have been read.
 759:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 760:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Additional information
 761:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    This function must not be called when J-Link might also do RTT.
 762:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    This function locks against all other RTT operations. I.e. during
 763:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    the read operation, writing is also locked.
 764:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    If only one consumer reads from the up buffer, 
 765:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    call sEGGER_RTT_ReadUpBufferNoLock() instead.
