 911:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** /*********************************************************************
 912:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 913:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_WriteSkipNoLock
 914:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 915:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 916:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT
 917:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    control block which is then read by the host.
 918:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_WriteSkipNoLock does not lock the application and
 919:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    skips all data, if the data does not fit into the buffer.
 920:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 921:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 922:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
 923:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
 924:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
 925:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *                 MUST be > 0!!!
 926:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *                 This is done for performance reasons, so no initial check has do be done.
 927:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 928:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
 929:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    1: Data has been copied
 930:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    0: No space, data has not been copied
 931:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 932:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
 933:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, all data is dropped.
 934:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
 935:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
 936:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
 937:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
 938:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** #if (RTT_USE_ASM == 0)
