1084:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1085:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
1086:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT
1087:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    control block which is then read by the host.
1088:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_WriteNoLock does not lock the application.
1089:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1090:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
1091:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
1092:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
1093:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
1094:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1095:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
1096:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
1097:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1098:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
1099:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) Data is stored according to buffer flags.
1100:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
1101:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
1102:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
1103:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
