1249:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1250:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
1251:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a single character/byte in SEGGER RTT buffer.
1252:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_PutCharSkipNoLock does not lock the application and
1253:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    skips the byte, if it does not fit into the buffer.
1254:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1255:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
1256:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
1257:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    c            Byte to be stored.
1258:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1259:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
1260:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
1261:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1262:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
1263:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, the character is dropped.
1264:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
1265:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
1266:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
1267:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
1268:./Application/Addition/RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
